{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788263948,"nonce":"sfhp6jxF+Bbz6fFjNQBtcokwql8=","message":"EVIDENCE FROM M1 — the absence of this spec is what made the run's work surface shallow. Session 13, verifying run `m1-20260831` (`664e9b9`).\n\n3.3 was listed as OPTIONAL on `664e9b9` (\"shelter may be dev-conjured\"). The ten-day run says that was the wrong call, and here is the measurement rather than the argument:\n\n- **`Alert_ColonistsIdle` was up for most of the run.** Three colonists, six in-game days, and nothing on the map generated construction work.\n- **Four dev-staged buildings were the entire colony for six days.** Nothing was ever added to it by player verbs, because no player verb can place a blueprint.\n- **A destroyed research bench could not be replaced.** This is the compounding one. `dev:spawn-thing` refused to place the bench at staging (`placed: 0`, journal seq 66 — see finding A on `664e9b9`), and once staging ended the no-dev-verbs invariant made the failure permanent. `Alert_NeedResearchBench` never cleared and research could not progress for the whole run. With 3.3 landed, that is a recoverable staging error; without it, a single silent refusal at tick 723 removes an entire subsystem for the rest of the run.\n\nThe general shape: a colony that cannot build can only consume what staging gave it. Every downstream loop 4.2 wants to exercise — production, expansion, defence geometry, recovery from loss — bottoms out on placing something. Idle colonists are the symptom.\n\nRaising the case for de-optionalising 3.3 before any M1 re-run. Not re-labelling the issue unilaterally; that is Evan's call, and it belongs on `664e9b9` where the dependency line lives.","files":null}]}